# UPS System Maintenance Procedure

## Equipment Information
- **UPS ID**: [UPS_ID]
- **Location**: Building [BUILDING], Floor [FLOOR], Room [ROOM]
- **Model**: [MODEL_NUMBER]
- **Serial Number**: [SERIAL_NUMBER]
- **Manufacturer**: [MANUFACTURER]
- **Installation Date**: [INSTALLATION_DATE]
- **Battery Date**: [BATTERY_DATE]

## Electrical Specifications
- **Input Voltage**: [INPUT_VOLTAGE] VAC
- **Output Voltage**: [OUTPUT_VOLTAGE] VAC
- **Power Rating**: [POWER_RATING] kVA
- **Battery Capacity**: [BATTERY_CAPACITY] Ah
- **Runtime**: [RUNTIME] minutes at full load

## Pre-Maintenance Checklist
- [ ] Notify IT department of maintenance window
- [ ] Verify backup power is available
- [ ] Check for any active alarms
- [ ] Ensure proper PPE is available
- [ ] Review previous maintenance records
- [ ] Verify work area is clear

## Maintenance Procedure

### 1. Visual Inspection
- Check for physical damage
- Verify all connections are tight
- Check for signs of overheating
- Inspect battery terminals for corrosion
- Verify ventilation is adequate

### 2. Electrical Testing
- **Input Voltage**: [INPUT_VOLTAGE] VAC ±5%
- **Output Voltage**: [OUTPUT_VOLTAGE] VAC ±2%
- **Frequency**: [FREQUENCY] Hz ±0.5%
- **Load Current**: [LOAD_CURRENT] A
- **Power Factor**: [POWER_FACTOR]

### 3. Battery Testing
- **Battery Voltage**: [BATTERY_VOLTAGE] VDC
- **Individual Cell Voltage**: [CELL_VOLTAGE] VDC
- **Battery Temperature**: [BATTERY_TEMP]°F
- **Load Test**: [LOAD_TEST] minutes
- **End Voltage**: [END_VOLTAGE] VDC

### 4. Transfer Testing
- **Normal to Bypass**: [NORMAL_TO_BYPASS] ms
- **Bypass to Normal**: [BYPASS_TO_NORMAL] ms
- **Normal to Battery**: [NORMAL_TO_BATTERY] ms
- **Battery to Normal**: [BATTERY_TO_NORMAL] ms

### 5. Alarm Testing
- **Low Battery**: [LOW_BATTERY_ALARM]
- **Overload**: [OVERLOAD_ALARM]
- **High Temperature**: [HIGH_TEMP_ALARM]
- **Communication**: [COMM_ALARM]

## Maintenance Schedule
- **Daily**: Visual inspection, alarm check
- **Weekly**: Load testing, temperature check
- **Monthly**: Battery voltage check, cleaning
- **Quarterly**: Full load test, calibration
- **Annually**: Complete system overhaul, battery replacement

## Safety Requirements
- **PPE Required**: Safety glasses, work gloves, hard hat, arc flash suit
- **Lockout/Tagout**: Required for all electrical work
- **Confined Space**: May apply for battery room
- **Hot Work**: Not applicable

## Emergency Procedures
- **Fire**: Activate fire suppression, evacuate area
- **Electrical Fault**: Open main disconnect, contact electrician
- **Battery Leak**: Isolate area, contact hazmat team
- **System Failure**: Switch to bypass, contact technician

